; NOTE on placement: weapon sections are patched through the SYSTEM namespace,
; so this file must be gamedata/configs/mod_system_*.ltx. A DLTX file named after
; the weapon ltx (mod_w_ar15_viper2_custom_hud_*.ltx) is never read and silently
; does nothing - that was the first attempt at this fix. 3DSS does the same thing
; the right way in mod_system_zz_3dss_ak104_alfa.ltx with ![wpn_ak104_alfa_hud].
;
; Viper 2 SuperCustom: the six "_off" HUD sections point at .ogf files that the
; mod does not ship. Flipping a magnifier or an offset sight switches the weapon
; to its _off section, the engine tries to load that model, and it is a hard
; FATAL in CModelPool::Instance_Load:
;
;   Can't find model file
;   'anomaly_weapons\wpn_ar15_viper2_custom\wpn_ar15_viper2_custom_e0t2_magd_off_hud.ogf'
;
; Confirmed 2026-10-29 by flipping the EOTech magnifier with the scroll wheel
; while aimed. All six are the same defect, so every flip on this weapon crashes,
; not just the EOTech one:
;
;   aim_t2_magd_off        Aimpoint T2 + magnifier
;   atacr_voodoo_off       ATACR + Voodoo offset mount
;   e0t2_magd_off          EOTech EXPS + FTC magnifier     <- the reported crash
;   e0t2_magd_unity_off    EOTech EXPS + magnifier, Unity mount
;   narcos_kit_off         Narcos kit
;   uh1_voodoo_off         UH-1 + Voodoo offset mount
;
; Every one is repointed at its own non-off model, which the mod DOES ship. The
; flip then plays its animation and changes the weapon's behaviour as normal,
; but the model does not visibly change: the magnifier stays drawn in line
; rather than folding aside. That is cosmetic. The alternative for the two
; EOTech rows is e0t2_hud.ogf, which drops the magnifier from view entirely but
; also drops its mount, so it pops worse. Swap them if you prefer that.
;
; The real fix is for the weapon pack to ship the six missing models.
;
; Unrelated and NOT fixed here: this pack also sets
;   custom_ui_func = magnifier_switch.on_hud_attach
; on three sections, and the magnifier_switch.script in 3DSS defines no such
; function. That is the
;   [wpn_...]: Script UI functor [magnifier_switch.on_hud_attach] does not exist!
; spam in the log. It is noisy, not fatal, and it is not what crashed the game.

